# KW09 - Metropolis
# Kraftwerk, score for the Casio VL-80 pocket calculator (1981),
# converted for the FA-1/FA-2 by Claude Code
#
# The score gives only the keys of the VL-80 and no note lengths: each
# note is an eighth note (Min), each blank between the groups of the
# score an eighth rest (MinF). The comment behind a line gives the keys
# of the VL-80 ("#" the semitone key). The VL-80 plays G3..A5 with the
# keys = . 0 1..9 ÷ × - + (operation manual, Manual Play Function).
# Program part, the note and tempo data are in KW09D. The
# FX-501P/FX-502P save program and data separately: load both, set
# the FA-1 to MUSIC, start the tape recorder and press P0.
# The FX-601P/FX-602P version is in fx602/KW09.prg.
# Total 35
# @calculator 502
# @number 709

*** P0
Min0 Min4 Min2 Min6 Min3 Min7 Min2 Min6 Min0 Min4  # keys [= 5 2 9 #2 #9 2 9 = 5 1 8 2 9 1 8]
Min1 Min5 Min2 Min6 Min1 Min5 MinF
Min0 Min4 Min2 Min6 Min3 Min7 Min2 Min6 Min0 Min4  # keys [= 5 2 9 #2 #9 2 9 = 5 1 8 2 9 1 8]
Min1 Min5 Min2 Min6 Min1 Min5 AC
